# 7 Sep 2026. Forward from d40ae3b1a97e, pinned yesterday. Diffed as a parsed
# schema tree rather than as text, because the last two defects on this
# document were both YAML that parsed cleanly into the wrong place
# (yuvoy-api#92, #103). PURELY ADDITIVE, and narrow: ONE endpoint changed.
# 28 lines added, none removed, nothing retyped.
#
# Consumed in this change (yuvoy-api#114):
#   - `GET /reels` now takes a `cursor` and answers with `complete` and
#     `nextCursor` — the same shape `/experiences` already had. This closes the
#     gap the previous pin recorded: the feed was one answer that stopped at 60
#     and could not say it had.
#
# The cursor is OPAQUE and must never be constructed. It carries the ROUND a
# reel is in for its own operator, then recency, then id — the three terms the
# ordering itself has. That is why a client cannot page this ordering: the
# rotation is computed across every eligible reel at query time, so resuming it
# from what the client holds restarts it, and one business's second reel
# arrives before another's first. The interleave is the one property the
# endpoint exists to protect.
#
# `complete` is TOLD, never inferred. A short page is not the end: a page that
# happens to come back exactly full would stop the scroll early, and an
# infinite scroll that has silently stopped looks identical to one with nothing
# more to show, so nobody reports it. `limit` is a page size now, not a feed
# size — the 60 cap is unchanged and no longer caps the feed.
#
# Landed earlier and still NOT consumed, each needing its own issue before
# anything is built:
